      <!-- FAQ -->
      <h2 class="mt-12 font-heading font-bold text-ink" style="font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.025em;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3 class="mt-8 font-heading font-semibold text-ink" style="font-size: 1.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Can a complete beginner join a group violin class?</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Yes, as long as the class is designed for beginners. A good beginner group assumes no experience, starts with how to hold the violin and bow, and moves at a pace that lets everyone build a foundation together.</p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 font-heading font-semibold text-ink" style="font-size: 1.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Do online group violin classes actually work?</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">They can, especially when the group is small and the class is live, so the teacher can see and respond to each person. They work best for building foundations and confidence. They can't replace the close, ongoing technical feedback of private lessons.</p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 font-heading font-semibold text-ink" style="font-size: 1.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">How small should a beginner group class be?</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Small enough that the teacher can genuinely see and hear each participant. With violin, details like bow angle and hand position matter early, so a smaller group usually means more useful feedback for everyone.</p>

      <h3 class="mt-8 font-heading font-semibold text-ink" style="font-size: 1.1rem; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Do I need my own violin before choosing a format?</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">Not necessarily. Some beginner courses don't require an instrument for the first session, and a teacher can help you find a well-fitted rental or purchase once you're ready. It's usually better to get advice first than to buy one in a hurry.</p>

      <!-- Local SEO closing section -->
